# The skill's interface, as two numbers (control-tower phase 98, #151).
# The console runs THESE scripts and tells every session to; the session reads
# SKILL.md from whatever copy of the skill Claude Code loaded — a plugin that
# can be many commits away. When one half grows a flag or a word the other
# rejects, a run goes wrong in the middle (`phase-outcome.sh verified`,
# `--boot-fanout` and `--verify-timeout` exited 2 against an older copy), so a
# run-start refuses first, naming the half to update.
#
# Plain KEY="VALUE" (sourced by bash 3.2), bare integers. Read by
# viewer/server/skill-copy.ts `readSkillApi`, for this copy and for the plugin
# copy a session under each config dir loads; an absent file is no verdict.
#
#   PE_API     — the interface these scripts speak. Raise it when a script
#                gains a flag, a subcommand or a word SKILL.md tells sessions
#                to use.
#   PE_API_MIN — the oldest interface of the OTHER half this one still works
#                with. Raise it when this copy starts relying on something an
#                older copy's scripts would reject. The console refuses a start
#                when the skill's PE_API is under the console's PE_API_MIN
#                ("update the skill"), and when the console's PE_API is under
#                the skill's PE_API_MIN ("update the console").
PE_API=1
PE_API_MIN=1
